  <!-- ============= Screen: Question 6 - changing antecedents =============== -->

  <Vertical id="bmod_h1_q6" title="6. Changing your antecedents">
    <Markdown id="bmod_h1_q6_prompt">
## 6. How could you change each antecedent?

By changing our antecedents we can change our behavior, and so our consequences
can change too.

For **each** of your two antecedents, describe how you could change it to get
closer to your goal behavior — then describe how that change would affect
**each** of your two consequences.

*For example: I am going to change my antecedent of sugar cravings (original A)
that leads to my drinking soda instead of water (UTB) by buying fruit-flavored
water at the grocery store (new A), which I hope will help me drink more water
(WGB). When I start buying it (new A), {{corpus:Q6/p7:affect_c1:49:72:sha=135811347528}} suffer from my
consequence of spending too much money on sodas (original C). Instead I will
have extra money {{corpus:PR/p2:pr:49:68:sha=043d19084034}} with friends (new C).*
    </Markdown>

    <Markdown id="bmod_h1_q6_recall">
**Your antecedents from 4a:**

1. {{@bmod_h1_q4a_first.value}}
2. {{@bmod_h1_q4a_second.value}}

**Your consequences from 4c:**

1. {{@bmod_h1_q4c_first.value}}
2. {{@bmod_h1_q4c_second.value}}
    </Markdown>

    <!-- Eight boxes, not two paragraphs.
         This item is scored on eight independent 1.25-point judgements: for
         each antecedent, is it named and does it match 4a, is the change to it
         described, is the affected consequence named and does it match 4c, is
         the effect described. Asking for it as two free paragraphs collapsed
         eight judgements into two boxes, which made the requirement something
         to remember rather than something to answer, and left the eight slots
         to be recovered from prose afterwards. One box per judgement makes each
         one askable, gradeable, and visible to the student as a thing they have
         or have not done. -->

    <Markdown id="bmod_h1_q6_a1_head">### Your first antecedent</Markdown>

    <Markdown id="bmod_h1_q6_state_a1_label">**Which antecedent from 4a are you changing?**</Markdown>
